# The repo's blobs are LF, and prettier (via eslint) enforces LF — but a Windows checkout
# with the default core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working tree, so every source
# file lints as one `Delete ␍` error per line and `next build` fails on a clean clone.
# Nothing in the diff is wrong; the checkout is. Pinning the working-tree ending here
# fixes it for everyone without asking each contributor to configure their client.
#
# Only the working tree changes: the stored blobs are already LF, so this produces no
# content diff. Existing Windows checkouts pick it up on their next checkout, or
# immediately via `git add --renormalize . && git checkout-index -a -f`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git must never translate or diff them as text. `text=auto` above already
# sniffs for this, but an explicit list costs nothing and does not depend on the sniff:
# a webp whose bytes happen to contain CRLF sequences is exactly the file that gets
# silently mangled when something decides it is text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
